SUMMARY:🚀 Starship | Starlink Group 31-2 (Starship Flight 15)
LOCATION:Orbital Launch Pad 2\, SpaceX Starbase\, TX\, USA
DESCRIPTION:Starship | Starlink Group 31-2 (Starship Flight 15)\n\nStatus
 \nTo be confirmed - date is likely but not final\n\nLift-off\n22:45 UTC\
 , Friday 13 November 2026\n\nProvider\nSpaceX\n\nSite\nOrbital Launch Pa
 d 2\, SpaceX Starbase\, TX\, USA\n\nOrbit\nLow Earth Orbit\n\nMission\n1
 5th test flight of the two-stage Starship launch vehicle and 4th flight 
 of Starship V3. Second Starship flight to deploy satellites (a group of 
 Starlink satellites known as Starlink Group 31-2) into stable Low Earth 
 Orbit and first ever to attempt returning the Starship 2nd stage back to
  the launch site. The ship is expected to fly at an altitude approximate
 ly 275 km above Earth and complete approximately 14 orbits around the pl
 anet for more than 22 hours\, with the ship expected to attempt returnin
 g back to Starbase\, Texas on its launch pad by pad arms catching. The b
 ooster’s primary test...\n\nLAUNCH DATES SLIP CONSTANTLY - weather\, t
 echnical holds and range availability move them\, often by days and some
 times by hours on the day itself. This calendar rebuilds daily\, but alw
 ays check before setting an alarm.
CATEGORIES:SpaceX,Starship
URL:https://nextspaceflight.com/launches/
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
STATUS:TENTATIVE
END:VEVENT
